1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,843
CHAPTER 6 — THE WIZARD

2
00:00:03,193 --> 00:00:10,731
In his New York laboratory, Tesla became a celebrity. One of his friends was the writer Mark Twain.

3
00:00:10,931 --> 00:00:17,777
They say he once invited him onto a vibrating platform. Before long, Twain went running to the bathroom.

4
00:00:17,977 --> 00:00:23,823
His signature tool was the Tesla coil. It works on something you've known since childhood.

5
00:00:24,273 --> 00:00:31,812
If you push a swing right as it comes back, gentle pushes send it higher and higher. That is resonance.

6
00:00:32,012 --> 00:00:39,550
The coil pushes electricity at the exact right moment. That's how it achieves huge voltages and multi-meter sparks.

7
00:00:39,750 --> 00:00:46,135
At an exhibition in New York, he placed an iron boat in a pool. With nobody inside.

8
00:00:46,335 --> 00:00:53,566
The audience shouted questions and the boat answered with its lights. Some believed he was controlling it with his mind.

9
00:00:53,766 --> 00:01:00,689
He was steering it with radio waves from a small box. It is the first radio-controlled device on record.

10
00:01:01,589 --> 00:01:06,050
Today we call it a remote control. And we use it to change the channel.
